        "html": "<h3 id=\"generating-surplus\">Generating Surplus</h3>\n<p>In summer, the village generates <button type=\"button\" class=\"dice-roll\" data-dice=\"1d4-1\" title=\"Click to roll 1d4-1 — Shift: advantage · Ctrl: disadvantage\">1d4-1</button> Surplus (from pickled spring vegetables, surplus winter potatoes, summer fruits, whisky maturing, game, etc.). If they also get a seasonal gain, the player can wait to pick it until they see how much Surplus they generate.</p>\n<p>When the autumn harvest is complete, the village gets another <button type=\"button\" class=\"dice-roll\" data-dice=\"1d4\" title=\"Click to roll 1d4 — Shift: advantage · Ctrl: disadvantage\">1d4</button> Surplus (crops, garden produce, game, mature livestock, etc.). Harvest is a process that takes most of autumn. If something significantly disrupts it, have the player roll for Surplus with disadvantage and/or a -1 penalty. If the harvest fails entirely, they don&#x27;t get any Surplus (and they Meet With Disaster).</p>",
